Hi Kristen,

Good to hear that you are making headway, but something is not quite right. You should only get the warning message about discarded observations if there were NAs for a covariate that did not correspond to NAs in the count matrix. Perhaps you could show us a printout of your unmarkedFrame (before you replaced missing values) if it's not too big.

There are many possible reasons for a singular hessian. Try reducing the number of covariates or using starting values based upon estimates from simpler models. I think this has been discussed on the list before.

Richard

