Thanks Dan,

I think I got it. I wasn't aware of the @Full option on the modSel object, I think that makes the difference. I will have to think about how my subsetting impacts the scaling of the AIC weights, so I may have to make a minor change.

Here's what I got:

require(unmarked);require(stringr)
modKira=modSel(fitKira)

## Grab the good models
good.models = lapply(as.list(modKira@Full$model[which(modKira@Full$cumltvWt<=0.955)]),get)
fitKira95 = fitList(fits=good.models)
modKira95 = modSel(fitKira95)

# Grab the model weights, coefficients for each model
weights = modKira95@Full$cumltvWt
coefKira = coef(modKira95)
coefKira[is.na <http://is.na>(coefKira)]=0
coefKira=coefKira[str_detect(names(coefKira),"psi")] ## Drop the detection parameters

# Derive the model averaged coefficients
coefmaKira=apply(coefKira*weights,2,sum) # Victory

It should be super easy to make this into a function. Many thanks again! I suppose I need to dig a little more into the internals.

Matthew

