References: <F4hTapERxOQ.XaZd-f3h54cJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/F4hTapERxOQ/m/b4V_stLpf0cJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

That's fairly straight forward:

If you take the example from the pcount function documentation accessed via:

?pcount

the code in there produces a no intercept model:

# Fit a model
fm1 <- pcount(~visit - 1 ~ x, umf, K=50)

the "-1" in the function call indicates that you don't want an intercept.

Cheers,
Richard S

